{"name":"Magician’s Cloak","hex":"#784467","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magician","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who plays with or practices allegedly supernatural magic.","A spiritualist or practitioner of mystic arts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magician"},{"term":"cloak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long outer garment worn over the shoulders covering the back; a cape, often with a hood.","A blanket-like covering, often metaphorical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover as with or like a cloak.","To cover up, hide or conceal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magician (fantasy)","blocks":[{"text":"A magician, also known as a mage, magus, magic-user, spellcaster, enchanter/enchantress, sorcerer/sorceress, warlock, witch, or wizard, is someone who uses or practices magic derived from supernatural, occult, or arcane sources. Magicians enjoy a rich history in mythology, legends, fiction, and folklore, and are common figures in works of fantasy, such as fantasy literature and role-playing games."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg/330px-The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magician_(fantasy)","wikidata":"Q148401"},{"title":"Cloak","blocks":[{"text":"A cloak is a type of loose garment worn over clothing, mostly but not always, as outerwear for outdoor wear, which serves the same purpose as an overcoat and protects the wearer from the weather. It may form part of a uniform. People in many different societies may wear cloaks. Over time, cloak designs have changed to match fashion and available textiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg/330px-Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak","wikidata":"Q516992"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Arthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG/500px-Arthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Arthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG/1280px-Arthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Arthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG/500px-Arthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Enchanter Merlin, by Howard Pyle, from The Story of King Arthur and His Knights (1903)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArthur-Pyle_The_Enchanter_Merlin.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Evelyn_De_Morgan_-_The_Love_Potion_%281903%29_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/500px-Evelyn_De_Morgan_-_The_Love_Potion_%281903%29_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Evelyn_De_Morgan_-_The_Love_Potion_%281903%29_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/1280px-Evelyn_De_Morgan_-_The_Love_Potion_%281903%29_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Evelyn_De_Morgan_-_The_Love_Potion_%281903%29_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/500px-Evelyn_De_Morgan_-_The_Love_Potion_%281903%29_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Love Potion by Evelyn De Morgan (1903)","link